<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jennifer Geerlings-Simons</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. 1953</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Jennifer Simons</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jennifer Geerlings-Simons is a Surinamese physician and politician who became the first woman president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suriname">Suriname</a> in July 2025. A leading member of the National Democratic Party founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/desi-bouterse">Desi Bouterse</a>, she was chairwoman of the National Assembly from 2010 to 2020 and was the party's candidate for the presidency after it came first in the elections of May 2025, when the National Assembly elected her.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jennifer-geerlings-simons.jpg" alt="Jennifer Geerlings-Simons" width="320" height="452" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lula Oficial · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jennifer_Geerlings-Simons,_November_2025.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
